From 14b21efecbb766aa3d947d780bd5ea7b8bcfd6f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MacScope contributors <contributors@macscope.invalid>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:03:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] test(gst): define external termio ABI and backend
 contract

Add the private external-I/O ABI v1 for host-fed terminal surfaces:
versioned size-prefixed C structs, fail-closed validation, result and
lifecycle enums, and callback typedefs in include/ghostty.h mirrored by
src/termio/External.zig.

The contract core is implemented and unit tested ahead of the backend
integration: the refcounted shared state with a bounded all-or-nothing
inbound mailbox (explicit byte and chunk capacities, atomic
backpressure), the validated host process-state machine (terminal
states latch, never regress, idempotent repeats), the latched
single-shot close request, and the fixed-size surface registry that
lets C entry points race safely with surface destruction (pin/drain
gate). Tests cover ABI validation fail-closed cases, forward-compatible
larger structs, byte-for-byte C header layout equality via the
translated ghostty.h module, feed copy/bound/atomicity semantics, the
process state machine, and registry bounds.

No backend integration yet: nothing constructs the external backend and
existing exec behavior is untouched.

